---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import {
  ReviewCardAgentSetup,
  ReviewCardAuthoring,
  ReviewCardBadges,
  ReviewCardComposition,
  ReviewCardConfirmation,
  ReviewCardPlayground,
  ReviewCardTableProposal,
  ReviewCardWorkflow,
} from "../../components/ReviewCardDemo";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<Docs
  title="Review Card"
  description="A card that asks someone to review a draft, approval, or table change before it runs, with facts, steps, an outcome, and decision buttons."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Review Card</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    Asks someone to review a proposed change in chat before it happens. The
    header names the change and its status and opens or closes the details. The
    footer holds the outcome and the decision buttons.
    <code>ReviewRows</code>, <code>ReviewSteps</code>, and
    <code>ReviewValues</code> lay out what will change.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8"><ReviewCardPlayground client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="A row change waiting for approval"
      code={`import { Database } from "reicon-react/icons/Database";
import {
  ReviewCard,
  ReviewRow,
  ReviewRows,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/review-card";

<ReviewCard
  label="Review row change"
  icon={<Database size={16} />}
  title="Update a row in Supplier deliveries"
  badge={{ label: "Needs approval", variant: "warning" }}
  settled={status !== "pending"}
  actions={
    <>
      <Button onClick={approve}>Approve change</Button>
      <Button variant="ghost" onClick={dismiss}>Dismiss</Button>
    </>
  }
  status={<p role="status">{outcome}</p>}
>
  <ReviewRows>
    <ReviewRow label="Change">Updates an existing row</ReviewRow>
    <ReviewRow label="Table">Supplier deliveries</ReviewRow>
  </ReviewRows>
</ReviewCard>`}
    />
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>icon</code>: a 14 or 16px icon shown in a tile before the title.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>badge</code>: <code>{"{ label, variant }"}</code>. The variant is <code
          >"warning"</code
        >, <code>"info"</code>,
        <code>"success"</code>, <code>"secondary"</code>,
        <code>"destructive"</code>, <code>"default"</code>, or
        <code>"outline"</code>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>settled</code>: the decision is made. The card folds to its header
        and footer, and folds again each time <code>settled</code>
        turns true. It opens again when <code>settled</code> turns false.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>status</code>: footer content that stays visible when folded, such
        as the outcome, feedback, or a status check.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>actions</code>: decision buttons. They show only while the card is
        open.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>label</code>: names the card, such as “Review row change”. Without
        it the title names the card.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Badge variants</h2>
    <div class="mt-4"><ReviewCardBadges client:load /></div>
    <p>
      Long titles end with an ellipsis; the badge and chevron keep their place.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Approval</h2>
    <p>
      An action that waits for approval. While submitting, both buttons are
      disabled and the chosen one shows a spinner. When settled, the card folds
      and focus moves to the outcome if the decision was made here.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4"><ReviewCardConfirmation client:load /></div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Drafts</h2>
    <p>
      Workflow, agent, and skill drafts share one card. Agent drafts list the
      change, team, model, actions, and skills; long instructions keep their
      line breaks. Feedback, technical details, and a status check sit below.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4"><ReviewCardAuthoring client:load /></div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Agent setup</h2>
    <p>
      Three decisions, with activation disabled until each consent box is
      checked. A sponsor conflict shows as an alert.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4"><ReviewCardAgentSetup client:load /></div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Workflow steps</h2>
    <p>
      <code>ReviewSteps</code> numbers each step. A step’s
      <code>detail</code> can hold <code>ReviewValues</code>, code, or notes.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Steps with exact values"
      code={`<ReviewSteps
  title="3 steps"
  steps={[
    {
      summary: "notify api: send POST to https://hooks.example.com/suppliers",
      detail: (
        <ReviewValues
          values={[
            { name: "content-type", value: "application/json" },
            { name: "Body", value: body },
          ]}
        />
      ),
    },
    { summary: "pause: wait 3600 seconds" },
  ]}
/>`}
    />
    <div class="mt-4"><ReviewCardWorkflow client:load /></div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Without actions</h2>
    <p>
      A table proposal whose values expired. It has no actions, only a status
      check, and scrolls inside a bounded area.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4"><ReviewCardTableProposal client:load /></div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Composition</h2>
    <div class="mt-4"><ReviewCardComposition client:load /></div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The card is a <code>section</code> named by <code>label</code> or the title.
      The title is an <code>h4</code> holding the button that opens and closes the
      details, with <code>aria-expanded</code>; the whole header is its click
      target, and its focus ring outlines the header. Enter and Space toggle it.
      The icon and chevron are hidden from assistive tech. Rows and values are
      description lists; steps are an ordered list under an <code>h5</code>,
      with the numbers hidden so screen readers use the list order.
    </p>
    <p>
      The details grow and shrink in 180ms and the chevron turns in 120ms; with
      reduced motion both happen at once.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      The card uses <code>--sprout-surface</code>,
      <code>--sprout-line</code>, <code>--sprout-canvas</code> for the icon tile,
      <code>--sprout-hover</code>, <code>--sprout-focus</code>,
      <code>--sprout-muted</code>, and <code>--sprout-secondary</code> for step numbers.
      Badges use the Badge tokens.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
